  "date": "2026-11-21",
  "category": "finance",
  "title_zh": "财政部：今年1到10月，全国财政收入接近20万亿元",
  "title_en": "Ministry of Finance: China's fiscal revenue nears 20 trillion yuan in January–October",
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "zh": "11月20日，财政部公布了今年前十个月的财政收支数据。从1月到10月，国家的一般公共预算收入是195671亿元，比去年同期增长了4.9%。一般公共预算收入是政府最主要的收入，大部分来自税收。",
      "en": "On November 20, the Ministry of Finance released fiscal revenue and spending data for the first ten months of this year. From January to October, national general public budget revenue was 19.5671 trillion yuan, 4.9% more than in the same period last year. General public budget revenue is the government's main type of income, and most of it comes from taxes."
    },
    {
      "zh": "其中，税收收入是162622亿元，增长了6%。国内增值税是最大的税种，收入超过6万亿元，增长5.3%；企业所得税超过4万亿元，增长5.9%。卖出股票时要交的证券交易印花税是2511亿元，增长了54.1%。",
      "en": "Of this, tax revenue was 16.2622 trillion yuan, up 6%. Domestic value-added tax, the biggest tax, brought in more than 6 trillion yuan, up 5.3%; corporate income tax brought in more than 4 trillion yuan, up 5.9%. Securities transaction stamp duty, which is paid when shares are sold, was 251.1 billion yuan, up 54.1%."
    },
    {
      "zh": "不过，和房子、土地有关的收入在减少。买房子时要交的契税下降了14.9%，土地增值税下降了16.6%。地方政府卖国有土地使用权得到的收入是18526亿元，下降了25.8%。",
      "en": "However, income linked to housing and land is falling. Deed tax, which is paid when buying a home, fell 14.9%, and land value-added tax fell 16.6%. Income that local governments got from selling the right to use state-owned land was 1.8526 trillion yuan, down 25.8%."
    },
    {
      "zh": "在支出方面，前十个月的一般公共预算支出是228042亿元，增长了1%。卫生健康支出增长得最快，达到7.8%；社会保障和就业支出增长了4.8%。",
      "en": "On the spending side, general public budget expenditure in the first ten months was 22.8042 trillion yuan, up 1%. Spending on health grew the fastest, by 7.8%; spending on social security and employment rose 4.8%."
    }
  ],
